# location-tracking-system

The location tracking system implements a multi-layered geolocation verification workflow for defendant compliance monitoring:

Core Location Verification Components:

1. GPS-Based Primary Tracking
- Consent-based GPS location capture 
- Accuracy radius calculation and validation
- Geographic compliance zone verification
- Automated timestamp correlation

2. IP Geolocation Fallback Chain
- Secondary location verification when GPS unavailable
- Provider fallback sequence for reliability
- VPN/proxy detection and filtering
- Last known location caching

3. Administrative Monitoring
- Geographic visualization of compliance zones
- Real-time location tracking with accuracy metrics
- Audit trail of location verification attempts
- Non-compliance detection and alerting

Location Data Flow:
```
GPS Request -> Accuracy Validation -> Zone Compliance Check -> Storage
     |
     v
IP Fallback -> VPN Detection -> Provider Verification -> Last Known Area
```

Key Business Rules:
- Location accuracy must meet minimum threshold for compliance
- Multiple verification attempts required for non-GPS sources
- Geographic zones defined by coordinate boundaries
- Timestamp verification for check-in validity
- Automated escalation for compliance violations

